From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 01:41:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 039/106] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150: add SoundWire TX wake
 interrupt

The WCD9375 codec sets wake_capable on its TX SoundWire link only.
qcom_swrm_probe() picks the wake interrupt up from index 1 of the
controller's interrupt list, so without a second entry the TX controller
has no wake IRQ at all.

The downstream sdmmagpie audio overlay (sdmmagpie is SM7150's downstream
name) lists the TX SoundWire interrupts as SPI 296 for the master and
SPI 500 for the wake. With the PDC's qcom,pdc-ranges = <0 480 94>, SPI
500 is PDC pin 20. Requesting it through the GIC directly does not map;
going through the PDC does.

Note that sdmmagpie also sets qcom,swr-wakeup-required = <0>, so
downstream does not arm this wake on SM7150; it is wired up here for
completeness because the codec driver advertises the link as wake
capable.

Signed-off-by: Edi <woodyst@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150.dtsi | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150.dtsi
index e7a28e8e7..1f0b4b611 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150.dtsi
@@ -4743,8 +4743,18 @@ lpass_tx_macro: codec@62ec0000 {
 		swr2: soundwire@62ed0000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,soundwire-v1.5.1";
 			reg = <0 0x62ed0000 0 0x2000>;
-			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 296 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-			interrupt-names = "core";
+
+			/*
+			 * The WCD9375 is wake_capable on the TX link only, and
+			 * the controller takes its wake interrupt from index 1
+			 * of this property. Downstream (sdmmagpie, which is what
+			 * SM7150 is called there) lists the TX SoundWire wake as
+			 * SPI 500; with qcom,pdc-ranges = <0 480 94> that is PDC
+			 * pin 20. It does not map through the GIC directly.
+			 */
+			interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 296 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+					      <&pdc 20 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupt-names = "core", "wakeup";
 			clocks = <&lpass_tx_macro>;
 			clock-names = "iface";
 			label = "TX";
-- 
